  "question": {
    "text": "$\\int_0^\\pi[\\cot x] d x,[\\bullet]$ denotes the greatest integer function, is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AnKFK",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "U3xkX",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MiRbT",
      "text": "\n$-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Pkjtq",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Let } \\mathrm{I}=\\int_0^\\pi[\\cot x] d x \\\\\n& =\\int_0^\\pi[\\cot (\\pi-x)] d x=\\int_0^\\pi[-\\cot x] d x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nAdding (1) and (2)\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& 2 I=\\int_0^\\pi[\\cot x] d x+\\int_0^\\pi[-\\cot x] d x==\\int_0^\\pi(-1) d x \\quad[\\because[x]+[-x]=-1 \\text { if } x \\notin Z \\\\\n& =[-x]_0^\\pi=-\\pi \\\\\n& \\therefore I=-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
